From f6a6aad0081f97c6124cb5e6171c42a44fcad9da Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: S&R Security Remediation <dev@sr-coresync.com>
Date: Sun, 1 Nov 2026 03:55:07 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 2/4] security(a1,a3,a4,a8): enforce auth, restrict CORS,
 harden upload, own sessions (P0-2)

- wire SovereignAuthMiddleware + SovereignRateLimitMiddleware into the app
  (CORS outermost so preflight works, then rate limit, then auth)
- CORS: allow_origins from CORESYNC_CORS_ORIGINS whitelist,
  allow_credentials=False, explicit methods/headers (A4)
- upload: content-length pre-check, max 5 files, streaming 1MB chunk reads
  with hard 5MB cap instead of full in-memory read (A3)
- sessions: owner column (auto-migration), ownership enforcement on
  history/delete, owner stamped on every message (A8)
- web/coresync-auth.js: frontend bridge adding X-API-Key to fetch calls
  and an EventSource helper for SSE channels
- .env.example: document all new CORESYNC_* security variables
